		{
			"to": "western-civ/si-redefinition",
			"why": "Millikan measured the Planck constant from the slope of Einstein's line to within about 1 per cent in 1916; in 2019 it was fixed at exactly 6.62607015 × 10⁻³⁴ J s and made to define the kilogram."
		},
		{
			"to": "feynman/cargo-cult",
			"why": "Millikan's value of h was his line's slope times his own oil-drop charge for the electron, the too-low value whose slow correction that frame follows, and it came out low with it."
		},
		{
			"to": "feynman/qed-book",
			"why": "Einstein's quantum of light is the photon of Feynman's QED, where a detector clicks one photon at a time and nothing predicts which photon will be reflected."
